title: watermark-eraser
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Burak
    family-names: Teke
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # Replace the ORCID above with yours, or delete the orcid line.
repository-code: "https://github.com/tekeburak/watermark-eraser"
url: "https://tekeburak.github.io/watermark-eraser/"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, privacy-first toolkit that removes AI provenance marks from
  content you own across three layers: invisible Unicode carriers (Layer A),
  statistical text watermarks via rewrite (Layer B), and C2PA/EXIF/XMP
  metadata across 16 file formats (Layer C). Stdlib-only core, hardened by
  design, with optional SynthID-Text self-verification, pixel-removal and
  scorer backends. Ships with an annotated watermarking research map,
  glossary and scheme taxonomy.
keywords:
  - watermarking
  - ai-provenance
  - c2pa
  - synthid
  - exif
  - xmp
  - privacy
  - unicode-security
  - python
  - cli
